                        "entry_id": "5accdb0a-f4f3-3761-83eb-1bd26ff717ae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lacking or (especially) opposed to reason and rational thought."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a64310a6-4ad9-4ebf-923d-f782172cae3b",
                                "sense_id": "0a865f22-fd33-3a91-b862-56a00dfd861b",
                                "text": "This view is further illustrated by bringing forward the Catholic doctrines, showing the “antirational notion of them,” and thus exhibiting “the mysterious bearings and incomplete character of the Revelation.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f92adda-cb00-4817-99fa-a1f5ca4165a4",
                                "sense_id": "0a865f22-fd33-3a91-b862-56a00dfd861b",
                                "text": "Rand refused to detach even a seemingly radical rebellion from the social totality in which it emerged. The New Left was as much an outgrowth of the antirational as the culture it had rejected."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89dc0a93-f837-4ee8-aa23-388161683201",
                                "sense_id": "0a865f22-fd33-3a91-b862-56a00dfd861b",
                                "text": "His own conception of a genuine (fifth order) postmodernism is not at all antirational and embraces everything that was a source of real strength in the fourth (“modern”) order of consciousness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
